extraStrings:
- type: en-US
  strings: &id001
    STR_COBRA_SIDEARM: Cobra Sidearm
    STR_COBRA_SIDEARM_UFOPEDIA: A heavy revolver, serial numbers ground off, bought by the crate on the civilian market. Cobra's first troops carry whatever handgun is cheapest. There is nothing to learn
      from the gun except that Cobra does not make its own yet.
    STR_COBRA_FIELD_RIFLE: Cobra Field Rifle
    STR_COBRA_FIELD_RIFLE_UFOPEDIA: An AK-pattern rifle, new and unissued, in a wooden stock with no country's markings. These are not scavenged. Someone is making rifles for Cobra in quantity, and the
      men who carried these were issued them, not given them.
    STR_COBRA_GRENADE: Cobra Grenade
    STR_COBRA_GRENADE_UFOPEDIA: 'Cobra''s fragmentation grenade: a simple, well-made design with a shorter fuse than ours. Roadblock thinks we can build it.'
    STR_COBRA_FIELD_KIT: Cobra Field Kit
    STR_COBRA_FIELD_KIT_UFOPEDIA: 'A Medi-Viper''s kit: pressure dressings, stimulants and a few drugs Doc had to send out to identify. Taken together they keep a wounded man fighting for longer than he
      should.'
    STR_COBRA_UNIFORM: Cobra Uniform
    STR_COBRA_UNIFORM_UFOPEDIA: The blue uniform, the snake on the helmet and the hood. The early cells wore whatever they owned with an armband; more and more of them now wear the full uniform. Each new
      uniform we see is a sign that Cobra's supply has reached that region.
    STR_FANG_WRECKAGE: F.A.N.G. Wreckage
    STR_FANG_WRECKAGE_UFOPEDIA: 'What is left of a Cobra F.A.N.G. gyrocopter: a small, cheap machine with a short range, a machine gun and rocket pods. It flies close to where it is based, which tells us
      a strip is nearby.'
    STR_STINGER_WRECKAGE: Stinger Wreckage
    STR_STINGER_WRECKAGE_UFOPEDIA: 'A Cobra Stinger: a four-wheel-drive jeep carrying a three-tube missile launcher. Built on a civilian chassis and fitted out somewhere with a good machine shop.'
    STR_VULTURE_PARTS: Vulture Parts
    STR_VULTURE_PARTS_UFOPEDIA: Wreckage from a Cobra Vulture, the cargo aircraft that carries Cobra's money, guns and men between sites. The cargo hold tells us what it carried; the navigation equipment
      tells us where it was going.
    STR_RATTLER_WRECKAGE: Rattler Wreckage
    STR_RATTLER_WRECKAGE_UFOPEDIA: 'A Cobra Rattler: a swing-wing ground-attack jet with a rear gun turret. It is built to hunt transports, not fighters. Our pilots will fly better against it now that they
      know how it turns, and our Skystriker can be improved from what we learned.'
    STR_HISS_WRECKAGE: H.I.S.S. Wreckage
    STR_HISS_WRECKAGE_UFOPEDIA: 'The first Cobra tank we have taken apart: the H.I.S.S., High Speed Sentry. Fast, lightly armoured, with twin cannons in an open turret. The hull plate carries a maker''s
      mark nobody here recognises.'
    STR_BAT_TEARDOWN: B.A.T. Teardown
    STR_BAT_TEARDOWN_UFOPEDIA: A Battle Android Trooper, taken apart on the bench. It is a machine, not a man in armour. Under the chest plate is a control chip that gives it its orders.
    STR_BAT_CONTROL_CHIP: B.A.T. Control Chip
    STR_BAT_CONTROL_CHIP_UFOPEDIA: The B.A.T.'s control chip, decoded. It takes orders by radio, which means a strong enough signal can confuse it, and it carries a factory code that points to where it
      was built.
    STR_RADIO_CODEBOOK: Radio Codebook
    STR_RADIO_CODEBOOK_UFOPEDIA: A Cobra radio codebook. Every intercept and coded paper we take from now on is quicker to read.
    STR_FUEL_RECEIPTS: Fuel Receipts
    STR_FUEL_RECEIPTS_UFOPEDIA: Fuel bought with cash at the same truck stops, again and again. A route.
    STR_VEHICLE_REGISTRATION: Vehicle Registration
    STR_VEHICLE_REGISTRATION_UFOPEDIA: The registration of a Cobra vehicle, to a company at an address. Small vans do not travel far from home.
    STR_MATCHBOOK: Matchbook
    STR_MATCHBOOK_UFOPEDIA: A matchbook from a business that does not seem to have any customers.
    STR_PHONE_NUMBER: Phone Number
    STR_PHONE_NUMBER_UFOPEDIA: A phone number written on a napkin. It rings at a house that is never answered and is never empty.
    STR_BURNED_PAPERS: Burned Papers
    STR_BURNED_PAPERS_UFOPEDIA: Papers somebody tried to burn and did not finish. What survived took a long time to read and was worth it.
    STR_CIRCLED_MAP: Map With a Place Circled
    STR_CIRCLED_MAP_UFOPEDIA: A road map with one place circled in pencil and a date beside it.
    STR_BANDED_CASH: Banded Cash
    STR_BANDED_CASH_UFOPEDIA: Cash in bank wrappers. The wrappers tell us which bank, and the bank tells us whose money it handles.
    STR_BILL_OF_LADING: Bill of Lading
    STR_BILL_OF_LADING_UFOPEDIA: 'A bill of lading for a cargo shipped by sea: a ship, a port and a date.'
    STR_TICKET_STUB: Ticket Stub
    STR_TICKET_STUB_UFOPEDIA: A bus ticket stub. The man who carried it came from a town on the route.
    STR_NOTICE_BOARD_ORDERS: Notice Board Orders
    STR_NOTICE_BOARD_ORDERS_UFOPEDIA: 'Orders pinned to a Cobra notice board: duty rosters and the next operation in the region.'
    STR_COBRA_PIN: Cobra Pin
    STR_COBRA_PIN_UFOPEDIA: A lapel pin with the Cobra emblem. Small, but it confirms who these men answer to.
    STR_PHOTOGRAPHS: Photographs
    STR_PHOTOGRAPHS_UFOPEDIA: 'Photographs of a meeting: faces, a car and a building we can find.'
    STR_COBRA_REVOLVER: Cobra Revolver
    STR_COBRA_RIFLE: Cobra Rifle
- type: en-GB
  strings: *id001
